# UrbanPulse Hackathon (FIICode)

Not every project needs to be a technical grind. Sometimes, you just want to do a side quest.

## What We Built

Entered the UrbanPulse hackathon with two friends who were semi-technical at best. The objective wasn't to write the cleanest code — it was to build something together, have fun, and survive the weekend.

## Technical Highlights

- Standard web stack: HTML, CSS, JavaScript — nothing fancy, just duct tape and caffeine
- Task delegation: Split work so everyone could contribute without getting overwhelmed
- Live debugging: Spent more time explaining web concepts and fixing teammates' CSS than writing my own logic

## What I Learned

This hackathon was 0% about technical growth and 100% about soft skills. Teaching beginners how web components work, keeping morale up when things broke, and maintaining patience when a teammate deleted a div and destroyed the layout — these are real project management skills. The code is forgettable, but the experience of leading a team through chaos was invaluable. Sometimes a side quest is exactly what you need.

